<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  Apple's privacy manifest, required for App Store submission.

  "Data Not Collected" (2026-10-12). The phone app collects nothing:

  - No sign-in. The phone, desktop and extension builds set @unisim/sdk's
    `noAccounts` (src/main.tsx, src/lib/accounts.ts), so there is no Universal
    ID, no email, no account id, and the SDK never reads a suite session the
    device holds (Keychain). No "the app was opened" event either: the SDK's
    <UsageTracker /> sends one only for a signed-in account.
  - No uploads. Signing and "Send for signature" happen on the phone: each
    "Sign here" box becomes a real PDF signature field and the file leaves
    through the system share sheet, to wherever the user sends it, never to
    us. The certified-signature route (stored copy, emailed link, certificate)
    is the website's only and is not in the phone app at all.
  - No usage count. The SDK's anonymous daily open count is off in the shell
    (`openCount: !isDesktop && !isNativeShell()`), and the suite user count it
    replaced (an install id) was retired in @unisim/sdk 0.187.0.
  - Signing on another phone (the QR handoff) relays the drawing as an
    ephemeral Realtime broadcast with a PIN: nothing is stored and nothing
    identifies the user, so it is not "collected" in Apple's sense.
  - The iOS Scan button is Apple's VisionKit (DocumentScanner.swift), which
    sends nothing. (The Android scanner's ML Kit diagnostics are declared in
    Play's Data safety answers, store-assets/data-safety.json; they do not
    apply here.)

  Nothing is used for tracking, and there are no third-party analytics or
  advertising SDKs.

  Required-reason APIs: @capacitor/filesystem reads file creation and
  modification dates (its `stat`), only on files in the app's own container,
  and it ships no manifest of its own. Capacitor's core frameworks carry their
  own manifests for what they use, so they are not repeated here.

  Keep this in step with the App Store Connect privacy answers ("Data Not
  Collected") and PRIVACY.md.
-->
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<!-- @capacitor/filesystem's stat: files in the app container. C617.1. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>C617.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
